commit ec123ddd0dcb86d2168d07ef0954ffae1dd9d9aa
Author: Cody Kang <codykang@vsit.ai>

dt-bindings: display: spacemit: add K3 Innosilicon DP/eDP controller

This commit adds the Device Tree binding schema for the SpacemiT K3
Innosilicon DisplayPort and embedded DisplayPort controller.

> diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/spacemit/spacemit,=
k3-inno-dp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/spacemit/spacem=
it,k3-inno-dp.yaml
> new file mode 100644
> index 0000000000000..491d25730da9f
> --- /dev/null
> +++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/spacemit/spacemit,k3-inno=
-dp.yaml
> @@ -0,0 +1,141 @@

[ ... ]

> +properties:
> +  compatible:
> +    const: spacemit,k3-inno-dp
> +
> +  reg:
> +    maxItems: 1
> +
> +  interrupts:
> +    maxItems: 1
> +    description: Link and hot-plug events.
> +
> +  clocks:
> +    items:
> +      - description: Pixel clock for the controller.
> +      - description:
> +          Pixel clock generated by the DP PHY PLL; the pixel clock above=
 is
> +          parented onto it in use.
> +
> +  clock-names:
> +    items:
> +      - const: pxclk
> +      - const: pll

[ ... ]

> +required:
> +  - compatible
> +  - reg
> +  - interrupts
> +  - clocks
> +  - clock-names

[ ... ]

> +        edp@cac84000 {
> +            compatible =3D "spacemit,k3-inno-dp";
> +            reg =3D <0x0 0xcac84000 0x0 0x4000>;
> +            interrupts =3D <132 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
> +            clocks =3D <&syscon_apmu CLK_APMU_EDP0_PXCLK>, <&edp0_phy>;
> +            clock-names =3D "pxclk", "pll";

[Severity: Low]
This isn't a bug, but DT binding schemas and example nodes follow the
canonical property ordering where clocks and clock-names appear before
interrupts.  Could interrupts be moved after clock-names in properties,
required, and the edp@cac84000 example node?

